      "description": "The one yellow action: call Ed, number on the second line.",
      "html": "<a class=\"ds-btn-call\" href=\"#\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" d=\"M5 3.5h3.2l1.6 4.2-2.2 1.4a11 11 0 0 0 5.3 5.3l1.4-2.2 4.2 1.6V17a2.5 2.5 0 0 1-2.7 2.5A15.5 15.5 0 0 1 2.5 6.2 2.5 2.5 0 0 1 5 3.5z\"/></svg><span class=\"ds-stack\">Call Ed<small>732-300-3835</small></span></a>",
      "css": ".ds-btn-call{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;min-height:76px;padding:14px 30px;border-radius:14px;border:3px solid var(--lane,#f5c242);background:var(--lane,#f5c242);color:var(--lane-ink,#132a1f);font-family:var(--font,system-ui);font-size:20px;font-weight:800;line-height:1.15;text-decoration:none;box-shadow:0 8px 22px -8px rgba(0,0,0,.55);transition:transform .2s cubic-bezier(.2,.8,.2,1)}.ds-stack{display:flex;flex-direction:column}.ds-stack small{font-size:17px;font-weight:700}.ds-btn-call:hover,.ds-btn-call:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--focus,#8fd6ff);outline-offset:3px}.ds-btn-call:active{transform:translateY(1px) scale(.99)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Outline Button",
      "kind": "button",
      "refersTo": "button-outline",
      "description": "Hero-only secondary beside the call button.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-sky\"><a class=\"ds-btn-line\" href=\"#\">Get my rate <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" d=\"M12 4v15M6 13l6 6 6-6\"/></svg></a></div>",
      "css": ".ds-sky{background:linear-gradient(180deg,#132849,#2c4770);padding:16px}.ds-btn-line{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;min-height:76px;padding:14px 30px;border-radius:14px;border:3px solid var(--white,#f7fbf8);background:rgba(19,40,73,.22);color:var(--white,#f7fbf8);text-shadow:0 1px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.45);font-family:var(--font,system-ui);font-size:20px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;transition:transform .2s cubic-bezier(.2,.8,.2,1)}.ds-btn-line:hover,.ds-btn-line:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--focus,#8fd6ff);outline-offset:3px}.ds-btn-line:active{transform:translateY(1px) scale(.99)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Sign Panel with Trip Rows",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "trip-row",
      "description": "The rate form sign panel; large single-column radio rows, selected fills lane yellow.",
      "html": "<fieldset class=\"ds-sign\"><legend class=\"ds-legend\">Your trip</legend><label class=\"ds-row\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"ds-t\" checked><span>New Jersey to Florida</span></label><label class=\"ds-row\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"ds-t\"><span>Florida to New Jersey</span></label></fieldset>",
      "css": ".ds-sign{margin:0;border:0;display:grid;gap:10px;background:var(--sign,#0d6a43);color:var(--white,#f7fbf8);border-radius:16px;box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 7px var(--sign,#0d6a43),inset 0 0 0 10px var(--white,#f7fbf8),0 18px 40px -18px rgba(0,0,0,.6);padding:30px 22px 28px;font-family:var(--font,system-ui)}.ds-legend{float:left;width:100%;font-size:20px;font-weight:800;margin-bottom:10px;padding:0}.ds-row{position:relative;display:block}.ds-row input{position:absolute;opacity:0;width:1px;height:1px}.ds-row span{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;min-height:64px;padding:10px 18px;border:2px solid rgba(247,251,248,.7);border-radius:12px;font-size:20px;font-weight:800;line-height:1.2;cursor:pointer;transition:background .15s,color .15s,border-color .15s}.ds-row span::before{content:\"\";flex:none;width:22px;height:22px;border-radius:50%;border:2px solid currentColor;box-sizing:border-box}.ds-row input:checked+span::before{border-width:7px}.ds-row input:checked+span{background:var(--lane,#f5c242);border-color:var(--lane,#f5c242);color:var(--lane-ink,#132a1f)}.ds-row:hover span,.ds-row input:focus-visible+span{outline:3px solid var(--focus,#8fd6ff);outline-offset:2px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Text Field",
      "kind": "input",
      "refersTo": "text-field",
      "description": "White field on the sign panel with a sentence-case label.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-field\"><label class=\"ds-lbl\" for=\"ds-car\">Your car</label><input class=\"ds-input\" id=\"ds-car\" placeholder=\"e.g. 2019 Toyota Camry\"></div>",
      "css": ".ds-field{background:var(--sign,#0d6a43);padding:16px;font-family:var(--font,system-ui)}.ds-lbl{display:block;color:var(--white,#f7fbf8);font-weight:800;font-size:20px;margin-bottom:10px}.ds-input{width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;min-height:58px;padding:14px 16px;font:inherit;font-size:19px;color:#10261c;background:var(--white,#f7fbf8);border:2px solid var(--white,#f7fbf8);border-radius:12px;caret-color:var(--sign,#0d6a43)}.ds-input::placeholder{color:#6f897d}.ds-input:hover,.ds-input:focus{outline:3px solid var(--focus,#8fd6ff);outline-offset:2px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "FAQ Item on Concrete",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "faq-item",
      "description": "Always-open question and answer; nothing collapses.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-qa\"><div><h3>Do you do airport runs?</h3><p>Yes, anywhere in Florida.</p></div><div><h3>Can I pack the car full?</h3><p>Yes. Your winter things ride along inside your own car.</p></div></div>",
      "css": ".ds-qa{background:var(--concrete,#e4e9e6);color:var(--concrete-ink,#0c3a2a);padding:16px;font-family:var(--font,system-ui)}.ds-qa>div{padding:20px 0;border-top:2px solid rgba(12,58,42,.18)}.ds-qa h3{margin:0;font-size:22px;font-weight:800;line-height:1.3}.ds-qa p{margin:8px 0 0;font-size:19px;line-height:1.55;color:var(--concrete-soft,#33584a);max-width:60ch}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Footer Close",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "footer-close",
      "description": "The close: shamrock, headline, Ed line, call button, tagline.",
      "html": "<footer class=\"ds-foot\"><h2>You fly. I'll drive.</h2><p class=\"ds-ed\">I'm Ed Brannagan, owner and driver of Shamrock Transportation.</p><p class=\"ds-tag\">&ldquo;Life is a Highway&hellip; Drive it All Night Long&rdquo;</p></footer>",
      "css": ".ds-foot{background:var(--ground-deep,#082a1e);color:var(--ink-soft,#cfe5d9);text-align:center;padding:56px 20px 44px;font-family:var(--font,system-ui);font-size:17px}.ds-foot h2{margin:0;font-size:clamp(1.7rem,7.6vw,2.8rem);font-weight:900;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:-.01em;line-height:1.02;color:var(--white,#f7fbf8)}.ds-ed{margin:14px auto 0;max-width:30ch;font-size:19px;color:var(--white,#f7fbf8)}.ds-tag{margin-top:20px;font-style:italic}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Posted Rate on I-95",
    "overview": "The page is the interstate at dusk, posted the way a highway posts things: a guide-sign green panel with an inset white rule, heavy retroreflective-white uppercase, readable at 65 mph and therefore readable by a 40-to-70 reader on a phone. It is short and calm on purpose: a hero with a self-driving road, one rate form on a sign panel, four always-open answers on concrete, and a dark footer that carries the close.\n\nDensity is low and the type is big. The ground is deep roadside green, never black; the one light section is highway concrete. Lane-line yellow is the one action color; a sky-blue outline is the one hover/focus voice. The hero road is the only thing on the page that moves.\n\nRejected by the build and the owner: stock truck photos, a quote-form wall, fine print, black grounds, webfonts, sticky bars, email links, accordions, anything a reader has to figure out.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One sign panel (green, inset white rule, 16px corners) holds the rate form.",
      "One yellow for action; one sky-blue outline for hover and focus.",
      "System font stack only, 800 to 900 and uppercase for headings; questions and controls in sentence case.",
      "One moving element: the hero road, driving itself slowly with gentle bends.",
      "Phone-first, big targets (58 to 76px controls), 17px text floor."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Never-Black Rule",
        "body": "The darkest surface is ground-deep. Black appears only inside soft shadows, never as a ground.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Yellow Rule",
        "body": "Lane yellow marks the action and the promise. A yellow surface is always a control (call button, selected trip row). Yellow text on green is either a link or the headline promise; plain instructions stay in white or soft white.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Outline Rule",
        "body": "Hover and focus on every control is a 3px focus-sky outline (offset 2 to 3px; 6px radius on text links). No other hover color, fill change or glow.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The 65 MPH Rule",
        "body": "No text on the page is under 17px, and nothing a reader acts on is lighter than 700.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No Webfont Rule",
        "body": "The system stack is mandatory. The canvas sign lettering reads the computed body font so drawn text matches the page.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Mounted Sign Rule",
        "body": "The only raised surface is a sign panel (and the yellow button). FAQ answers and footer content stay flat, divided by rules, not cards.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** keep the hero road as the page's only moving element; everything else is still apart from short color and press transitions.",
      "**Do** put the rate form on a sign panel with the Sign Mount treatment.",
      "**Do** use the 3px #8fd6ff outline for every hover and focus.",
      "**Do** keep controls 58px or taller, answer choices as large single-column rows, and all text at 17px or larger.",
      "**Do** show answers in full; a question and its answer sit together on the page.",
      "**Do** keep yellow text on green to links and the headline promise."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** make the road (or anything) react to touch, drag or pointer, and don't add a second animation.",
      "**Don't** use accordions, tabs, carousels or other hide-and-reveal patterns.",
      "**Don't** use black or neutral charcoal as any ground; the darkest is ground-deep.",
      "**Don't** load a webfont; the system stack is the brand type.",
      "**Don't** add a sticky header or sticky bottom call bar, or email links.",
      "**Don't** put more than two buttons in the hero, or make the second anything but the outline.",
      "**Don't** style non-clickable things as clickable: no yellow fills or bordered rows on anything that isn't a control.",
      "**Don't** place lane-yellow on concrete.",
      "**Don't** use hard offset shadows; depth is the soft sign mount."
    ]
  }
}
